/-
FL4 differences (PORTING.md, "FL4 differences"): **the extended kernel
with FL4's VMEnter report** (FL4 #80 / #81 / #85; `Ext/VirtReport`).

`fl4CallKernelVF onCore remoteCur rep ev` is `fl4CallKernelV onCore rep
ev` (`Ext/VirtKernel`) with every VMEnter completion as FL4 main
279c8261 does it: `vmCheckF` at the exit and after a guest step,
`vmEnterF` for `SysVMEnter`, `vcpuDetachF` in finalisation (VCPU caps,
final thread caps) and SetTCB (`associateVcpuTcbF`), and `sendSignalVF`
in every signal (interrupts, the notification invocation, the TCB
timers). `remoteCur t` (FL4 `node_get(cpu, CUR_THREAD) == t` for `t`'s
core `cpu`) is, like `onCore`, a per-core fact the uniprocessor spec does
not have, fixed for the entry.

Each definition here is its `Ext/VirtVcpu` / `Ext/VirtFinalise` /
`Ext/VirtEntry` / `Ext/VirtDispatch` / `Ext/VirtKernel` namesake (suffix
`F`) with these substitutions only; the module is generated by
`proofs/scratch/virt12/genTopF.py` (head `topF_head.lean`).

The ported modules and the `V` definitions are not changed.
-/
